fix: death cures a poison still on its way (poison.rs2)

Not a bot hunk: an upstream bug (Content 274, also in 289). A poison splat that kills leaves the
death for the next tick (the queue's last entry); a poisonous NPC's hit in that tick (its %death
check still false) queues poison_player behind the death. clear_poison cleared poison_damage but not
poison_player, so the player was poisoned again at Lumbridge ("You have been poisoned!"). It now
clears both; its other caller, the end of a duel, also drops a poison still queued.

diff --git a/scripts/skill_combat/scripts/poison.rs2 b/scripts/skill_combat/scripts/poison.rs2
index e043e14..8f5f852 100644
--- a/scripts/skill_combat/scripts/poison.rs2
+++ b/scripts/skill_combat/scripts/poison.rs2
@@ -63,6 +63,7 @@ if (stat(hitpoints) = 0) {
 
 [proc,clear_poison]
 clearqueue(poison_damage);
+clearqueue(poison_player);
 %poison = 0;
 cleartimer(poison);
 
